1
00:00:00,008 --> 00:00:01,583
Welcome to Cafe Manager.

2
00:00:01,583 --> 00:00:16,419
This video walks you through everything your front desk needs: starting and billing timed sessions, locking PCs and switching off console TVs when time runs out, members and prepaid time, food and drinks, receipts and reports.

3
00:00:16,769 --> 00:00:22,297
Everything runs on one computer inside the cafe, so it keeps working even when the internet is down.

4
00:00:23,251 --> 00:00:24,344
First, logging in.

5
00:00:25,097 --> 00:00:28,280
Open the Cafe Manager address on the front desk computer.

6
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,736
Your owner will usually bookmark it for you.

7
00:00:31,088 --> 00:00:33,988
Type the shared staff password and press Log in.

8
00:00:33,988 --> 00:00:39,970
After five wrong tries in five minutes, that device is blocked for five minutes, so take your time.

9
00:00:40,322 --> 00:00:41,023
The dashboard.

10
00:00:41,776 --> 00:00:43,763
The dashboard is your home screen.

11
00:00:43,763 --> 00:00:51,183
Every station in the cafe has its own card, and the cards update live, so every screen at the desk always shows the same thing.

12
00:00:51,534 --> 00:00:59,178
The badge in the corner shows the status: Idle means free, In session, Paused, Expiring when time is nearly up, or Offline.

13
00:00:59,529 --> 00:01:05,086
Console stations also show the TV status, with buttons to switch the TV on or off.

14
00:01:05,086 --> 00:01:09,763
There is no real TV connected in this demo, so they show Unreachable.

15
00:01:10,113 --> 00:01:14,451
In the bottom corner of this video you can see the screen of a gaming PC.

16
00:01:14,451 --> 00:01:17,481
Right now it is locked, waiting for the front desk.

17
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:24,569
One more thing: press Enable sound once at the start of your shift, so you hear the alarm when a station runs out of time.

18
00:01:24,921 --> 00:01:25,827
Starting a session.

19
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:28,763
A customer wants one hour on PC 3.

20
00:01:28,763 --> 00:01:36,083
On the card, press one of the quick buttons: thirty, sixty, a hundred and twenty, or a hundred and eighty minutes.

21
00:01:36,434 --> 00:01:40,484
The PC unlocks within a second, and the countdown starts on the card.

22
00:01:40,484 --> 00:01:42,949
The charge is shown and updates as you go.

23
00:01:43,299 --> 00:01:46,338
For any other length, type the minutes in the box and press Start.

24
00:01:46,691 --> 00:01:47,882
Extending and pausing.

25
00:01:48,634 --> 00:01:49,836
They want more time?

26
00:01:49,836 --> 00:01:55,124
Press plus fifteen, plus thirty or plus sixty, or type your own number and press Extend.

27
00:01:55,124 --> 00:01:57,348
The new time goes straight to the PC.

28
00:01:57,699 --> 00:01:59,941
If a customer steps out, press Pause.

29
00:01:59,941 --> 00:02:03,697
The clock stops, the PC locks, and paused time is not charged.

30
00:02:04,048 --> 00:02:05,385
Press Resume when they are back.

31
00:02:05,737 --> 00:02:07,623
Members and open-ended sessions.

32
00:02:08,375 --> 00:02:14,228
To attach a customer, search by name or phone number in the customer box, and pick them from the list.

33
00:02:14,579 --> 00:02:18,039
Alex is a member, so the member rate is applied automatically.

34
00:02:18,391 --> 00:02:21,809
Press Start open ended when the customer will pay at the end.

35
00:02:21,809 --> 00:02:25,731
The clock counts up instead of down, and it never runs out on its own.

36
00:02:26,081 --> 00:02:28,448
Customers can also buy prepaid hours.

37
00:02:28,448 --> 00:02:30,815
Jordan has five hours on his balance.

38
00:02:31,167 --> 00:02:34,532
Pick Jordan, check the minutes, and press Start from balance.

39
00:02:34,532 --> 00:02:37,896
The time is taken from the balance instead of being paid now.

40
00:02:38,249 --> 00:02:39,132
Moving a session.

41
00:02:39,884 --> 00:02:43,077
A PC has a problem, or friends want to sit together?

42
00:02:43,077 --> 00:02:46,271
Choose a free station under Move to, and press Move.

43
00:02:46,271 --> 00:02:50,692
The session carries on at the new station with the same time and charge.

44
00:02:51,045 --> 00:02:52,579
Controlling a PC remotely.

45
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:56,667
Every PC card has a menu with three dots.

46
00:02:56,667 --> 00:03:02,133
From here you can lock or unlock the PC, restart it, shut it down, or send a message.

47
00:03:02,486 --> 00:03:05,182
Let's tell PC 3 that their noodles are ready.

48
00:03:09,344 --> 00:03:14,043
The message pops up in the corner of the customer's screen, without interrupting their game.

49
00:03:14,395 --> 00:03:15,500
When time runs out.

50
00:03:16,253 --> 00:03:20,441
Now the most important part: what happens when paid time runs out.

51
00:03:20,441 --> 00:03:25,009
Let's start a very short one minute session on PC 1, so we can watch it.

52
00:03:25,361 --> 00:03:29,864
Before the end, the customer sees a countdown in the corner of their screen.

53
00:03:29,864 --> 00:03:33,598
Warnings are shown at ten, five and one minutes before the end.

54
00:03:33,598 --> 00:03:37,331
At the desk, the station appears in the alert strip at the top.

55
00:03:37,682 --> 00:03:40,424
Press Acknowledge to tell the rest of the team you have seen it.

56
00:03:45,501 --> 00:03:49,450
At zero, the card shows Time up and a short grace period begins.

57
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:53,646
The customer's countdown turns red, telling them to save their work.

58
00:03:53,646 --> 00:03:58,150
If they want more time, just press Extend now and nothing is interrupted.

59
00:04:04,354 --> 00:04:07,313
When the grace period ends, the PC locks itself.

60
00:04:07,313 --> 00:04:10,149
For a console, the TV is switched off instead.

61
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:16,932
And this also works if the network goes down: the PC keeps counting on its own and still locks at zero.

62
00:04:16,932 --> 00:04:20,553
The amount owed is waiting on the POS page as an open tab.

63
00:04:20,905 --> 00:04:22,270
Stopping and taking payment.

64
00:04:23,022 --> 00:04:23,873
PC 3 is done.

65
00:04:23,873 --> 00:04:24,594
Press Stop.

66
00:04:24,594 --> 00:04:30,030
The panel shows the final charge, including any food and drinks added to their tab.

67
00:04:30,382 --> 00:04:32,465
Press Stop and settle to take payment now.

68
00:04:32,816 --> 00:04:34,252
You can split a payment.

69
00:04:34,252 --> 00:04:40,296
Here the customer pays five dollars in cash, so choose Cash, enter the amount, and press Add payment.

70
00:04:40,648 --> 00:04:43,878
Then press Rest by card for the remainder, and Record payment.

71
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:47,904
The payment is saved and a receipt number is created.

72
00:04:47,904 --> 00:04:49,765
You can print it, or press Done.

73
00:04:49,765 --> 00:04:51,336
The PC locks straight away.

74
00:04:51,688 --> 00:04:55,381
If someone will pay later, press Stop, then Stop, pay later.

75
00:04:55,381 --> 00:04:58,582
The amount stays on an open tab until it is settled.

76
00:04:58,934 --> 00:04:59,798
Food and drinks.

77
00:05:02,514 --> 00:05:05,023
Open the POS page to sell food and drinks.

78
00:05:05,023 --> 00:05:09,982
Tap a product to add it to the cart, and use plus and minus to change the quantity.

79
00:05:10,334 --> 00:05:12,643
For a walk-in customer, press Charge now.

80
00:05:12,643 --> 00:05:16,979
When paying cash, type what they hand you, and Cafe Manager shows the change.

81
00:05:20,566 --> 00:05:26,844
To put items on someone's session instead, choose Active session, pick the station, and press Add to tab.

82
00:05:26,844 --> 00:05:30,073
It will be added to their bill when the session stops.

83
00:05:30,423 --> 00:05:32,366
Open tabs are listed on the right.

84
00:05:32,366 --> 00:05:37,165
Press Settle to take payment for any of them, like the session that expired earlier.

85
00:05:37,517 --> 00:05:38,914
Customers and packages.

86
00:05:41,644 --> 00:05:45,075
On the Customers page you can search, add and edit customers.

87
00:05:45,075 --> 00:05:46,987
Tick Member when you add a member.

88
00:05:47,339 --> 00:05:51,840
Open a customer to see their balance, purchases, receipts and recent sessions.

89
00:05:52,192 --> 00:05:56,075
To sell a package of hours, choose the package and press Sell package.

90
00:05:56,075 --> 00:06:00,679
Take the payment, and the minutes are added to their balance as soon as it is paid.

91
00:06:01,031 --> 00:06:02,211
Sessions and reports.

92
00:06:04,921 --> 00:06:10,473
The Sessions page lists every session, with its start and end, why it ended, and what it cost.

93
00:06:10,473 --> 00:06:13,957
Press Events to see exactly what happened during a session.

94
00:06:16,286 --> 00:06:23,558
Reports show the money collected for any period: today, this week, this month, or a custom range, split into cash and card.

95
00:06:23,910 --> 00:06:30,689
Scroll down for revenue by day and week, by station type, by product and category, and by payment method.

96
00:06:30,689 --> 00:06:34,627
Every table can be exported to a spreadsheet with Export CSV.

97
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:36,058
Setup, for the owner.

98
00:06:36,811 --> 00:06:40,170
The pages under Setup are normally used by the owner only.

99
00:06:42,488 --> 00:06:46,508
Station types set the hourly price, with an optional cheaper member price.

100
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:52,066
Stations is where each PC and console is added.

101
00:06:52,066 --> 00:06:55,243
A PC is linked to its agent by its machine ID.

102
00:06:55,243 --> 00:07:01,113
A console needs the TV's network address, and is paired once with the Pair TV button.

103
00:07:03,433 --> 00:07:07,860
Products are the food and drinks sold on the POS page, grouped by category.

104
00:07:10,167 --> 00:07:14,926
Packages are prepaid bundles of hours, for one station type or for any station.

105
00:07:17,233 --> 00:07:23,708
Rate rules change the price at certain times, for example a weekend evening price, or a cheaper rate in the morning.

106
00:07:26,019 --> 00:07:35,785
Settings holds the grace period and warning times, the key used to connect gaming PCs, the TV power-off option, the receipt printer, and the nightly backups.

107
00:07:36,137 --> 00:07:37,256
If something goes wrong.

108
00:07:39,967 --> 00:07:46,186
If a PC card says Agent offline, check that the PC is switched on and connected to the network.

109
00:07:46,186 --> 00:07:48,018
It will reconnect by itself.

110
00:07:48,018 --> 00:07:52,863
If a TV shows Unreachable, check it is plugged in and on the cafe network.

111
00:07:53,214 --> 00:08:00,090
And if a PC is ever stuck locked with the server down, staff can use the emergency unlock code on the lock screen.

112
00:08:00,090 --> 00:08:01,779
Ask your owner for the code.

113
00:08:01,779 --> 00:08:04,855
The full staff guide is included with the software.

114
00:08:05,208 --> 00:08:05,689
That's it.

115
00:08:05,689 --> 00:08:08,291
You are ready to run the front desk with Cafe Manager.
